t.  After her 2000 gold medal, she won the silver medal at the 2001 World Championships in the middleweight division.  But in 2003, she moved up to the heavyweights, earning a bronze medal at the Worlds.  Her biggest competition was expected to come from France’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/94105"} "Myriam Baverel"] ", who had competed in this class in Sydney, finishing =8th.  Baverel had been the runner-up as a middleweight at the 2003 World Championship.  Both had tough early draws.  Chen faced " [:a {:href "/athletes/94168"} "Adriana Carmona"] " of Venezuela in the quarters.  Carmona was 2003 Pan-Am champion and had finished =5th in this division in Sydney, but Chen defeated her, 7-5.  Baverel had to face Canada’s defending bronze medalist, " [:a {:href "/athletes/94082"} "Dominique Bosshart"] ", in the first round, but prevailed 7-5.  Baverel won in the quarters and semis only by superiority each time.  The final was not close, as Chen crushed Baverel 12-5.  Carmona won the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/94084"} "Chen Zhong"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/94105"} "Myriam Baverel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/94168"} "Adriana Carmona"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/VEN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; ve